      "message": "line 136 applies to input objects, and this applies to resulting fips_module.o.  I didn\u0027t notice impact from line 136 though, but added it mostly to be sure that it doesn\u0027t produce native code (-fno-fat-lto-objects) and if some reordering happens, it won\u0027t affect next stages - documentation on -frandom-seed is rather poor and not clear wherever it should be used for inputs or outputs. I didn\u0027t notice any difference with this option too. Looks like we just remove sections it impacts on.\n\nMost code size impact was from -flto-partition\u003d1to1 and -fipa-pta. Both can be added to whole image build probably. Code blocks reordering sometimes makes smarter choices removing extra branches, but I noticed that explicitly setting -O1 for these functions does the same. Something -O2/-Os does hurts tight loops frequently.",
